    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing our highest offensive floor; his 87.42 score is fueled by a stellar 0.449 xwOBA and an advantageous matchup against Melton. We are leaning heavily into speed-driven upside today, highlighted by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (76.65). Despite a middling matchup against Peralta, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a mandatory start due to his elite stolen base potential, compounded by a 4% efficiency boost stemming from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery to the plate. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (72.81) earns a high-leverage spot; while the park factor is slightly suppressive, his 13% SP Skill advantage against Lugo makes him the premier anchor for the middle of our order.\n\nPlatoon edges are dictating the back half of our lineup, with **Lars Nootbaar** (62.94) and **Colt Keith** (62.77) both benefiting from positive splits against right-handed pitching. We are monitoring a 42% rain risk for **Lars Nootbaar**, but his high efficiency score keeps him locked in unless a late-hour cancellation is announced. Conversely, **Caleb Durbin** remains a marginal play (46.70) despite his elite speed profile; his score is dragged down by the 17% SP Skill penalty imposed by Schlittler. **Pedro Ramirez** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench with a 43.04 score; the optimizer favored the higher raw offensive production of **Luke Raley** and the category-specific weight of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, leaving **Pedro Ramirez** as our primary depth piece should a weather delay strike **Lars Nootbaar** or **Kyle Schwarber**.",
